&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;#LI-RH1&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dive in and do the best work of your career at DigitalOcean. Journey alongside a strong community of top talent who are relentless in their drive to build the simplest scalable cloud. If you have a growth mindset, naturally like to think big and bold, and are energized by the fast-paced environment of a true industry disruptor, you’ll find your place here. &amp;nbsp;We value winning together—while learning, having fun, and making a profound difference for the dreamers and builders in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;We want people who are passionate about enabling the teams they work with to effectively and efficiently deliver value in line with the DigitalOcean vision.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Program Manager on the Physical Infrastructure team, you will drive value delivery for a set of technical programs and special projects that bring our cloud and AI infrastructure to life, spanning data center build-outs, hardware deployment, capacity across our global fleet, and the operational initiatives that keep it all running. This individual will be a cross-functional collaborator who champions continuous improvement and thrives in a fast-paced environment, applying technical literacy along with relevant experience to navigate delivering on commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will partner with Product, Engineering, and infrastructure teams to drive the delivery of valuable technical programs that scale our agentic inference cloud and meet our customers&#39; heavy compute needs. You will connect the work across the internal teams and outside vendors that get infrastructure online, embodying servant leadership to ensure efficient, effective value delivery. You will be a proactive collaborator while driving consensus where needed and influencing decisions when teams are stuck. A real part of this job is the steady, behind-the-scenes work of keeping people on track: following up, closing loops, and making sure commitments made in a meeting still hold down the line. You&#39;ll bring a growth mindset to all of it, prioritizing learning and improvement for yourself and the teams you work with, communicating the &quot;why&quot; behind change, and building learning cycles into how the team works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At any given time, you may be working on projects ranging in variety from brand new hardware deployments, to new hiring and onboarding initiatives; from a Finance partnership in need of critical infrastructure context, to an expansion of datacenter capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive value delivery across your assigned programs and special projects, including prioritization, planning, risk management, execution, and measurement of success. You&#39;ll own delivery of your programs and deliverables with guidance from your manager and senior TPMs, and lead defined workstreams on larger, more complex programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and infrastructure leads throughout the life of the program on value delivery and process/practice improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep supply chain, facilities, hardware engineering, colocation providers, remote hands, and internal networking teams informed and aligned on the schedules for your programs, coordinating the steps from site and capacity planning through deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships within and across teams to lead stakeholders toward a common goal; facilitate team and cross-functional meetings that foster decision-making across multiple teams and locations, and help your team prioritize work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and often about program requirements, timelines, objectives, status, risks, technical concepts, and process, so that expectations are understood and supported by both internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the follow-through on your programs: tracking commitments across teams and vendors, checking in before a date slips, and closing the loop on open questions and decisions so nothing falls through the cracks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help your team identify, capture, and manage risks, recognizing risk early, whether a delayed hardware shipment or a facility constraint, and forming mitigation plans as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage changes in scope and priority shifts, and aid in resolving impediments, conflicts, and competing priorities for your team and across teams, working unplanned issues to resolution with support as appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suggest improvements to team processes and help implement the repeatable ways of working (and the visibility behind them) that get infrastructure online faster and improve reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Add to DigitalOcean:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core to the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience keeping cross-functional work on track in a fast-paced environment: planning it, spotting what&#39;s about to slip, resolving what blocks it, and driving it to done. You don&#39;t need to have held the &quot;Technical Program Manager&quot; title; we&#39;re interested in people who&#39;ve done this work under other names, including project or delivery management, data center or deployment operations, facilities or construction project management, supply chain or capacity planning, and technical business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personable yet persistent, with authentic interpersonal interactions. You&#39;re comfortable being the person who follows up, and follows up again, without wearing out your welcome&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of what qualifies as a risk, and how to capture and manage risks appropriately for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify and clearly state problems that arise within your team, think critically about the stated need versus the underlying cause, gather necessary data, and to suggest and help implement solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distill complex or technical concepts into clear, structured communications and action plans, balancing a detail- and process-oriented mindset with a focus on outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and facilitation skills: building productive relationships and managing expectations, looking for areas of agreement, and hearing the concerns that go unvoiced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence and work through others where direct reporting relationships do not exist, acting as a bridge between deeply technical teams and operational teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools to take the toil out of your daily work, whether drafting and tightening status communications, summarizing long threads and meetings, or synthesizing scattered information into a clear picture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Also valuable:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in physical infrastructure, hardware, facilities, or data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the infrastructure context: data center and hardware fundamentals such as rack space, power, cooling, and deployment workflows; the procurement lifecycle and its long lead times; and the basics of the AI/ML hardware space, including why customers use GPUs and the high-level difference between training and inference. Depth in all of these isn&#39;t expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management tooling (e.g., the Atlassian suite/Jira and Confluence), including creating and updating items, dashboards and basic querying, and building roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Range:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$98,000 - $122,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;*This is a hybrid role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;JR: 2026-8201&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Why You’ll Like Working for DigitalOcean&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We innovate with purpose. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll be a part of a cutting-edge technology company with an upward trajectory, who are proud to simplify cloud and AI so builders can spend more time creating software that changes the world. As a member of the team, you will be a Shark who thinks big, bold, and scrappy, like an owner with a bias for action and a powerful sense of responsibility for customers, products, employees, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We prioritize career development.&lt;/strong&gt; At DO, you’ll do the best work of your career. You will work with some of the smartest and most interesting people in the industry. We are a high-performance organization that will always challenge you to think big. Our organizational development team will provide you with resources to ensure you keep growing. We provide employees with reimbursement for relevant conferences, training, and education. All employees have access to LinkedIn Learning&#39;s 10,000+ courses to support their continued growth and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We care about your well-being.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Regardless of your location, we will provide you with a competitive array of benefits to support you from our Employee Assistance Program to Local Employee Meetups to flexible time off policy, to name a few. While the philosophy around our benefits is the same worldwide, specific benefits may vary based on local regulations and preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We reward our employees. &lt;/strong&gt;The salary range for this position is based on market data, relevant years of experience, and skills. You may qualify for a bonus in addition to base salary; bonus amounts are determined based on company and individual performance. We also provide equity compensation to eligible employees, including equity grants upon hire and the option to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;DigitalOcean is an equal-opportunity employer. &lt;/strong&gt;We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, national origin, caste, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, age, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic makeup, marital status, or military service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Application Limit:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;You may apply to a maximum of 3 positions within any 180-day period. This policy promotes better role-candidate matching and encourages thoughtful applications where your qualifications align most strongly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dive in and do the best work of your career at DigitalOcean. Journey alongside a strong community of top talent who are relentless in their drive to build the simplest scalable cloud. If you have a growth mindset, naturally like to think big and bold, and are energized by the fast-paced environment of a true industry disruptor, you’ll find your place here. &amp;nbsp;We value winning together—while learning, having fun, and making a profound difference for the dreamers and builders in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DigitalOcean is looking for a Senior Software Engineer, Network Datapath to help build and evolve the software that powers high-performance networking across our cloud infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of networking, operating systems, distributed systems, and high-performance software, developing datapath technologies that enable DigitalOcean to deliver high throughput, low latency, and predictable network performance at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will focus on the software running in and around the network datapath, including packet processing, forwarding, routing, acceleration, observability, and integration with host and hardware-based networking components. You will work closely with Network Infrastructure, Compute, Availability, and hardware teams to design, implement, optimize, and operate production networking systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a strong software engineer with deep networking knowledge who enjoys working close to the system and is excited about optimizing the path that packets take through cloud infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and optimize high-performance network datapath software for DigitalOcean&#39;s cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve packet-processing and forwarding systems with a focus on throughput, latency, CPU efficiency, scalability, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop networking functionality across the host, kernel, user space, and hardware-accelerated datapath.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technologies such as Linux networking, eBPF, XDP, DPDK, AF_XDP, SR-IOV, and programmable datapaths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze packet-processing paths and identify opportunities to eliminate bottlenecks and improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop software for routing, packet filtering, encapsulation, tunneling, load balancing, traffic steering, and network virtualization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve datapath observability, telemetry, debugging, and performance monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design software that integrates with DPUs, SmartNICs, programmable NICs, and other hardware acceleration technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automated testing and benchmarking frameworks to validate datapath correctness and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate complex production networking issues, including packet drops, latency, throughput degradation, CPU utilization, and unexpected traffic behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Network Infrastructure and Compute engineers to integrate datapath functionality into DigitalOcean&#39;s broader infrastructure architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design and implementation of next-generation network architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author RFCs, architecture documents, technical proposals, design documents, and implementation plans to drive complex networking initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly document technical decisions, tradeoffs, performance characteristics, dependencies, and operational considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews and provide technical guidance to other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and contribute to improving software engineering and networking practices across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience designing and developing production software in C, C++, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking and packet processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing software for Linux-based networking systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of networking concepts including TCP/IP, routing, switching, VLANs, VXLAN, BGP, ECMP, NAT, load balancing, and network virtualization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging and optimizing performance-sensitive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Linux networking internals, including the Linux kernel networking stack, network namespaces, sockets, queues, interrupts, and NIC drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more high-performance networking technologies such as DPDK, XDP, eBPF, AF_XDP, or SR-IOV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multithreaded and concurrent software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of performance analysis, profiling, benchmarking, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to reason about complex systems across hardware, operating systems, networking, and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently drive projects from technical design through implementation and production deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical writing skills, with the ability to produce RFCs, architecture/design documents, technical proposals, and other documentation required to drive engineering projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to work effectively across engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with hardware-accelerated networking is highly valuable. This includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing software for DPUs, SmartNICs, IPUs, or programmable NICs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding how functionality can be distributed between host CPUs, NICs, DPUs, and switches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DPU-based networking, security, storage, virtualization, or packet processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with programmable datapaths such as P4, eBPF, or other programmable data-plane technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of PCIe, DMA, queues, interrupts, RSS, offloads, and NIC hardware architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the Senior Engineer level, you will be expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own significant technical components and deliver them from design through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex performance and reliability problems in the network datapath.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound technical decisions based on measurable performance and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable solutions rather than one-off fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify architectural and performance bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work effectively across Network Infrastructure, Compute, Security, and other engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear RFCs and technical documentation that enable teams to align on complex architectural decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and raise the technical bar within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and modern engineering tools to increase personal and team leverage and accelerate delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on cloud networking or hyperscale infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing Linux kernel networking code or NIC drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DPDK, XDP, eBPF, AF_XDP, or DPU-based datapaths in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with 400G+ networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-performance packet processing at 10/25/40/100/200/400G+ speeds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with network virtualization and overlay technologies such as VXLAN/EVPN.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with programmable switches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance analysis using tools such as perf, eBPF tooling, flame graphs, or hardware performance counters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building network datapath tests and benchmarking infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to Linux, DPDK, eBPF, OVS, or other networking/open-source projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why DigitalOcean&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role provides an opportunity to work on some of the most performance-sensitive software in DigitalOcean&#39;s infrastructure. The network datapath is foundational to the performance, scalability, and reliability of our cloud platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help shape the evolution from traditional host-based networking toward highly optimized, programmable, and hardware-accelerated datapaths, while solving challenging problems across software, operating systems, networking, and hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Range:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;$167,200 - $209,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;*This is a remote role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;JR: 2026-8151&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Why You’ll Like Working for DigitalOcean&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet p-rich_text_list--nested&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-list-tree=&quot;true&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We innovate with purpose. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll be a part of a cutting-edge technology company with an upward trajectory, who are proud to simplify cloud and AI so builders can spend more time creating software that changes the world. As a member of the team, you will be a Shark who thinks big, bold, and scrappy, like an owner with a bias for action and a powerful sense of responsibility for customers, products, employees, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We prioritize career development.&lt;/strong&gt; At DO, you’ll do the best work of your career. You will work with some of the smartest and most interesting people in the industry. We are a high-performance organization that will always challenge you to think big. Our organizational development team will provide you with resources to ensure you keep growing. We provide employees with reimbursement for relevant conferences, training, and education. All employees have access to LinkedIn Learning&#39;s 10,000+ courses to support their continued growth and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We care about your well-being.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Regardless of your location, we will provide you with a competitive array of benefits to support you from our Employee Assistance Program to Local Employee Meetups to flexible time off policy, to name a few. While the philosophy around our benefits is the same worldwide, specific benefits may vary based on local regulations and preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;We reward our employees. &lt;/strong&gt;The salary range for this position is based on market data, relevant years of experience, and skills. You may qualify for a bonus in addition to base salary; bonus amounts are determined based on company and individual performance. We also provide equity compensation to eligible employees, including equity grants upon hire and the option to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;DigitalOcean is an equal-opportunity employer. &lt;/strong&gt;We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, ancestry, national origin, caste, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity or expression, age, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, genetic makeup, marital status, or military service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
